#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:12
msgid "Hub learns about Satellites in two ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Managed (config + systemd)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Declare a process in `~/.anima/config.yaml`. `anima service start/stop/restart` writes `anima-satellite-<name>.service` user units (when systemd is available) and starts/stops them with `anima.service`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"satellites:\n"
"  pair-programming:\n"
"    enabled: true\n"
"    command: bun\n"
"    args: [\"satellites/pair-programming/dev.ts\"]\n"
"    env:\n"
"      STUDIO_WORKSPACE: /path/to/project\n"
"      SATELLITE_PORT: \"4173\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Chat / Task / Admin** etc. are bundled in shell-ui (desktop / mobile / web); no separate `satellites:` dev process needed; browser local debug: `bun run dev:web`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field              | Role                                             |\n"
"| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| `command` / `args` | Process to run (required for managed satellites) |\n"
"| `env`              | Extra environment variables                      |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:36
msgid ""
"Working directory is derived by anima from the install layout (monorepo root "
"or CLI package root), not configured here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Startup:** managed satellites start only after Hub `GET /api/health` returns `status: ok`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:40
msgid ""
"See [service.md](../guide/service.md) for systemd unit paths and startup "
"order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic (SAP connect)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:44
msgid ""
"No `command` in config. Start the satellite yourself; it connects to Hub via "
"SAP WebSocket. Instances appear on Admin → Satellites after connect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:46
msgid "There is **no** global `studio:` section in `config.yaml`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:48
msgid ""
"Open managed satellite UI at the URL from Admin (SAP `http_url`), typically:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:50
msgid "Pair-programming: `http://127.0.0.1:4173`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:52
msgid ""
"Shell satellites (Chat, Admin, etc.) open in desktop / mobile / web shell "
"routes; no dedicated port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instance allocation strategies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:56
msgid ""
"`instance_id` is a 3-character lowercase alphanumeric id (see [`packages/sap-"
"contract/src/naming.ts`](../../packages/sap-contract/src/naming.ts)). It "
"appears in platform strings (`sap:{app_slug}:{instance_id}`), session "
"`platform_extra`, and SAP tool names. **Do not remove it from the protocol** "
"— but each satellite app picks an **allocation strategy** suited to its "
"product model:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Strategy      | Meaning                                | Apps                                        | Client behavior                                                                 |\n"
"| ------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **singleton** | One fixed id per Hub for the whole app | **Chat** (`def`)                            | Always send `instance_id` on `connect`; Hub auto-provisions if missing          |\n"
"| **machine**   | One id per physical device / install   | **Companion**, **pair-programming** (today) | Omit `instance_id` on first connect; Hub assigns randomly; persist locally      |\n"
"| **workspace** | One id per open workspace / project    | **Pair-programming** (future)               | Switch workspace → switch `instance_id` and reconnect — **not implemented yet** |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart TB\n"
"  subgraph policies [Allocation strategies]\n"
"    Singleton[\"singleton: chat → def\"]\n"
"    Machine[\"machine: companion → per machine\"]\n"
"    Workspace[\"workspace: pair-programming → per project future\"]\n"
"  end\n"
"  Singleton --> Platform1[\"platform = sap:chat:def\"]\n"
"  Machine --> Platform2[\"platform = sap:companion:{machineId}\"]\n"
"  Workspace --> Platform3[\"platform = sap:pairprogramming:{projectId}\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Chat (singleton):** all desktop / mobile clients share `CHAT_INSTANCE_ID` (`def`) so `conversation.list` is unified across devices. Chat registers no satellite tools; multiple devices may connect with the same id (Admin shows the last `http_url`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Companion (machine):** `~/.anima/companion/instance.json` — one id per computer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pair-programming (machine today):** single sidecar + `STUDIO_WORKSPACE` at startup → one `~/.anima/satellites/pair-programming/instance.json`. When runtime workspace switching ships, migrate to **workspace** strategy (separate instance per project).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:82
msgid ""
"Hub [`SapInstanceRegistry`](../../platform/src/sap/instance-registry.ts): "
"omit `instance_id` → random allocation; send known id → reconnect or **auto-"
"provision** if the id is valid and unused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "Satellite access modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Rule:** each `app_id + instance_id` has **at most one** active entry in `SatelliteManager` (last connect wins). Multiple WebSockets with the same id are not rejected but stream events follow each socket's own context.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Type B — Process gateway + local relay (pair-programming)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:93
msgid ""
"Sidecar `createSatelliteHub({ relay: true, ... })` holds the sole Hub WS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:93
msgid "Browser uses `createSapRelayBrowserClient` → satellite `/sap/relay/v1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:93
msgid ""
"`instance_id` persisted under `~/.anima/satellites/{app}/instance.json`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:93
msgid "**Pair-programming:** relay + `tool.register` + local FS/PTY APIs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "SAP direct — browser/renderer connects to Hub (chat embedded in app/desktop)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:99
msgid ""
"Renderer uses [`createSapDirectClient`](../../packages/sap-contract/src/"
"direct-client.ts) to connect to Hub `/sap/v1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:99
msgid ""
"**No** relay sidecar; Chat uses **singleton** fixed `instance_id` "
"(`CHAT_INSTANCE_ID` = `def`), no per-device persistence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:99
msgid "See [`frontend-exports.md`](frontend-exports.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Type B + tools, no relay (companion)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:105
msgid ""
"Sidecar `createSatelliteHub({ relay: false, tools: [...] })` holds the sole "
"Hub WS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:105
msgid ""
"Browser talks to sidecar HTTP only (no SAP relay); tools execute in sidecar "
"(`bubble`, `play_slot`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:105
msgid ""
"`instance_id` in `~/.anima/companion/instance.json`; platform `sap:companion:"
"{id}`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/satellite-guide.md:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart TB\n"
"  subgraph chat [Chat Type B relay]\n"
"    B1[Browser] -->|relay WS| Relay1[\"/sap/relay/v1\"]\n"
"    Relay1 --> ProcSAP1[createSatelliteHub]\n"
"    ProcSAP1 -->|single SAP WS| Hub1[Hub]\n"
"  end\n"
"\n"
"  subgraph ppy [Pair-programming Type B]\n"
"    B2[Browser] -->|relay WS| Relay2[\"/sap/relay/v1\"]\n"
"    Relay2 --> ProcSAP2[createSatelliteHub]\n"
"    ProcSAP2 -->|single SAP WS| Hub2[Hub]\n"
"    B2 --> LocalFS[\"/api/studio/*\"]\n"
"    B2 --> LocalPTY[local terminal WS]\n"
"    ProcSAP2 --> ToolExec[tool executor]\n"
"  end\n"
msgstr ""

